<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110716" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθῑσήνωρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ορος</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθίω, ἀνήρ</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>destroying</i> or <i>killing men,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.833
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				9.604
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				431
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.457
				</span></i>
			. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ</span> perh. metri gr.,
			but in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.833
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθεισ-</span> is found in some codd.
			(including <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὰ τῶν παλαιῶν
			ἀντιγράφων</span> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				356.20
			</span></i>), and <i><span class="en">
				Choerob.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.Ox.</u>
				2.273
			</span></i>, and shd. perh. be read.]</div>
